sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Morphometric validation: 22/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "spectral_ring_metrics computes k*, wavelength, ring sharpness and azimuthal m2/m4/m6 harmonics on the cortical fields and writes them to the CSV, and the Gaussian-only control is a quantitative model-level check. -25: none of these numbers is compared with a value measured on a specimen or reported in the literature (no hypercolumn spacing in mm, no ring spacing in degrees of visual angle, no Klüver/Rule psychophysical statistic). -15: k* equals the preset's wave_count (12, 14, 24) by construction and the self-test threshold k* >= 6 is trivially met, so the metric validates the renderer's input, not the model. -12: the CSV's max(m4, m6) column is 0.95-0.99 for every preset including pure rolls (a single roll has |c_m| = 1 for all m), so the lattice-symmetry discriminator does not discriminate. -14: the one metric that does compare against a digitised paper figure, the Floquet source-curve RMS (0.154) in rule-2011-floquet.json, is read into floquet_overlap_rms but never printed or plotted, and upstream marks it outside threshold; the metrics are computed on the cortical sheet only, never on the retinal pullback that is the actual claimed form constant. Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L769–L812: spectral metrics computed on cortical field; no reference values anywhere <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L769-L812>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1316–L1321: self-test only requires k* >= 6; k* is wave_count by construction <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1316-L1321>; bressloff_v1_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): kluver rows: k* = 14/12/12/24 = wave_count; m4_m6 column 0.954-0.986 for rolls and lattices alike — bressloff_v1_metrics.csv: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at 68c4a1a, text/csv, 1508 B, artifact_sha256 2b6efe3a19972d59918b8fd9d2000a5eee12b9093a7cf407e1fa5171f0324294 (sha256 2b6efe3a19972d59918b8fd9d2000a5eee12b9093a7cf407e1fa5171f0324294), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1194–L1196: floquet_overlap_rms read from fixture but never surfaced; upstream fit_objective has calibration_claim_allowed=false <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1194-L1196>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): bressloff-v1-form-constants stability_reports parity, max |Δ| = 0.0 dimensionless (reference 0.0, MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants commit 344863a1bd9e8a8e8c9cb20aced2897f3ffb2c4c) [maximum absolute error across all 5 Bressloff (2001) stability_reports (q*, λ*, γ(0), γ(θ), η_hex) vs paper-calibration.json]; Mexican-hat lateral inhibition critical wavenumber q* (Bressloff 2001 Fig. 16) = 1.028 dimensionless wavenumber (reference >0.5 (finite Turing/Euclidean symmetry-breaking wavelength), Bressloff et al. 2001 Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 356:299 Fig. 16) [maximizer of max(λ_even(q), λ_odd(q)) with lateral_inhibition = 0.27] — interior peak prominence = 0.1200; Gaussian-only negative control critical wavenumber q* (lateral_inhibition = 0) = 0.05 dimensionless wavenumber (reference 0.05, q_min boundary of [0.05, 3.0] grid (monotonically decaying dispersion, prominence = 0.0)) [maximizer of λ(q) when Mexican-hat surround inhibition is removed (lateral_inhibition = 0.0)] — interior peak prominence = 0.00e+00; Klüver Tunnel/Rings cortical planform spectral ring sharpness = 30.556 ratio (peak/median PSD) (reference >5.0, Bressloff et al. 2001 Fig. 7 / Klüver 1966 Tunnel form constant) [2D FFT radial power spectrum peak/median ratio at k* = 14 cycles]; Klüver Honeycomb/Hex cortical planform spectral ring wavenumber k* = 24.0 cycles / domain (reference >0, Bressloff et al. 2001 Fig. 35 / Klüver 1966 Honeycomb form constant) [dominant radial FFT wavenumber of the 3-mode hexagonal cortical planform] — ring sharpness = 7.76." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.22"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Morphometric validation' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dct:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary) + Gemini 4 Argon (independent blinded second assessor)" .
}

sub:provenance {
    sub:assertion prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00336965>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2000.0769>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1162/089976602317250861>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002158> .
    <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00336965> dct:date "1979"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "A mathematical theory of visual hallucination patterns" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2000.0769> dct:date "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "Geometric visual hallucinations, Euclidean symmetry and the functional architecture of striate cortex" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1162/089976602317250861> dct:date "2002"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "What geometric visual hallucinations tell us about the visual cortex" .
    <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002158> dct:date "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
        dct:title "A model for the origin and properties of flicker-induced geometric phosphenes" .
}

